      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-244548",
      ":question/problem": "![](images/e5/e58ae4bec5e7b0b4788576ac8ef2f9ad6286269134d6cbda9a3be316b4751f79.png)\n\nIn the diagram above, $KL^(\u2015)\u22a5JK^(\u2015)$ and $KL^(\u2015)\u22a5MN^(\u2015)$.\n\nConsider the following statement:\n\n> $\u25b3JKL\u223c\u25b3MNL$\n\nThe table below gives the proof of the statement. Select the correct options in the table and thus complete the proof.\n\n|  | Statement | Reason |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| 1 | $\u2220L\u2245\u2220L$ | Reflexive property of congruence |\n| 2 | $KL^(\u2015)\u22a5JK^(\u2015)$ | Given |\n| 3 | $KL^(\u2015)\u22a5MN^(\u2015)$ | Given |\n| 4 | $\u2220K$ is a right angle | {{field-1}} |\n| 5 | {{field-2}} | Definition of perpendicular lines |\n| 6 | $\u2220K\u2245\u2220MNL$ | {{field-3}} |\n| 7 | $\u25b3JKL\u223c\u25b3MNL$ | {{field-4}} |"
